From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Laferriere <9342524+samlaf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 11:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drivers/acpi: log only the accesses the BadAML sandbox denies

The sandbox logs every SystemMemory access AML makes, allowed or not.
Azure's AML makes about 8200 reads on every boot, and on a serial console
each line costs about 4 ms, which comes to over 40 s of boot.

Log only denied accesses. They are the ones that mean something, and the
line for each is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Samuel Laferriere <samlaf92@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/acpi/acpica/sandbox.h | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/acpi/acpica/sandbox.h b/drivers/acpi/acpica/sandbox.h
--- a/drivers/acpi/acpica/sandbox.h
+++ b/drivers/acpi/acpica/sandbox.h
@@ -135,12 +135,14 @@
 {
 	cond_resched();
 
+	if (__sandbox_access_log.access_allowed)
+		return;
+
 	ACPI_INFO((
-		"SANDBOX: ACCESS %s virt=%lx phys=%lx %s",
+		"SANDBOX: ACCESS %s virt=%lx phys=%lx denied",
 		__sandbox_access_log.is_read ? "r" : "w",
 		(unsigned long)__sandbox_access_log.virt_addr,
-		(unsigned long)__sandbox_access_log.phys_addr,
-		__sandbox_access_log.access_allowed ? "allowed" : "denied"
+		(unsigned long)__sandbox_access_log.phys_addr
 	));
 
 	cond_resched();
-- 
2.49.0

